{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for your Amplitude project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the API key, posts to the HTTP V2 endpoint of the project’s data residency ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":", and splits each batch to Amplitude’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 10 events and 1 MB a request, which a project on any plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepts. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The API key goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leaves this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in Amplitude’s default data center or its EU","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and an event posted to the other doesn’t reach it, so you pick the region on purpose. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for an empty key, and for an Amplitude Experiment deployment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key, which isn’t the project’s API key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous device. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that session’s start in Unix milliseconds; a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context aren’t sent, nor is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the standard context is sent as Amplitude’s own fields","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Amplitude counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and bills by monthly tracked users, so each session counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one tracked user, and so does each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with, into"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Amplitude keeps for its own ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Amplitude] …"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$identify"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$groupidentify"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import AmplitudeEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: amplitude)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Amplitude receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"AmplitudeEncoding","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Amplitude","title":"Sending to Amplitude"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"},"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}]},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeRegion":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeRegion"}],"title":"AmplitudeRegion","abstract":[{"text":"The data center an Amplitude project’s data resides in, which decides the HTTP V2 endpoint its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events are posted to.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeRegion"}],"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplituderegion","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeRegion"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncodi